# Line-ending policy.
#
# REDACTS verifies its threat-knowledge data files against SHA-256 digests
# recorded in threat_base/data/checksums.json. Git's autocrlf translation
# rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which changes those digests and makes the
# loader abort with:
#
#     INTEGRITY FAILURE: yaml/<file> has been tampered with.
#     This file may have been maliciously modified to bypass security
#     detection rules.
#
# On Windows (core.autocrlf=true, the installer default) that fired on every
# fresh clone - telling an analyst their detection rules may have been
# tampered with when only the line endings had changed. Marking these paths
# `-text` keeps them byte-identical on every platform so the digests hold.
#
# Do not remove these rules without also changing how checksums are computed.

threat_base/data/yaml/*.yaml   -text
threat_base/data/yara/*.yar    -text
threat_base/data/checksums.json -text

# Detection fixtures are matched byte-wise by YARA and the regex rules; keep
# them stable across platforms for the same reason.
tests/data/php/**              -text

# Captured CLI output is reproduced verbatim in the user guide.
docs/captures/*.txt            -text
